        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anil Kumar, Rajat Gupta\n- Companies: McKinsey & Company, Goldman Sachs, Procter & Gamble, American Airlines\n- Organizations: Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation, The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria\n- Places: Silicon Valley, India\n- Roles: senior partner, director, board member, advisor\n- Systems: Internet practice\n\nFacts:\n- Anil Kumar, born in 1958, was a senior partner and director at McKinsey & Company.\n- At McKinsey & Company, Anil Kumar co-founded the firm's offices in Silicon Valley and India.\n- At McKinsey & Company, Anil Kumar created the Internet practice, which represented a quarter of the firm's business at the time.\n- Rajat Gupta served as a board member of Goldman Sachs, Procter & Gamble, and American Airlines.\n- Rajat Gupta served as an advisor to the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation and The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria.",
